# SPEED (same box, 2 cores shared with a place-and-route; user time ~ wall)
# old bench: ~275k-400k half-clocks/s (load dependent); fast driver: ~280k-420k half-clocks/s. Gain 1.0-1.1x, NOT the 3x asked for.
# Instructions/s: using the issue's ratio 23k instr/s per 372k half-clocks (0.062 instr/half-clock): ~17k-26k instr/s for both.
# Projected full run at ~400k half-clocks/s: 3.5e9 ref instr / 0.062 = 5.7e10 half-clocks / 4e5 = ~40 h (unchanged by the driver).
#
# PROFILE (gprof, -O2 build of the fast driver, group 13, 1.5M posedges; perf is not permitted here: perf_event_paranoid=4)
# Time is in the generated core logic, not the bench or scheduler:
#   Flat profile:
#   
#   Each sample counts as 0.01 seconds.
#     %   cumulative   self              self     total           
#    time   seconds   seconds    calls  ns/call  ns/call  name    
#    53.04      1.31     1.31  3000003   436.67   436.67  Vz80_system___024root___ico_sequent__TOP__0(Vz80_system___024root*)
#    35.22      2.18     0.87  1500000   580.00   580.00  Vz80_system___024root___nba_sequent__TOP__0(Vz80_system___024root*)
#     2.43      2.24     0.06  6000002    10.00    10.00  Vz80_system___024root___eval_phase__act(Vz80_system___024root*)
#     2.02      2.29     0.05  6000004     8.33   228.33  Vz80_system___024root___eval_phase__ico(Vz80_system___024root*)
#     1.62      2.33     0.04  1500000    26.67    26.67  Vz80_system___024root___nba_sequent__TOP__1(Vz80_system___024root*)
# ___ico_sequent (combinational pass after inputs change) 53% and ___nba_sequent (flop updates + comb) 35%: ~88% of time, ~2.2 us per posedge.
# Scheduler/eval overhead (eval_phase__act/ico, VlDeleter, msg queue) is ~7%. Skipping the clk=0 eval (design has only posedge logic) saved ~30% over a plain two-eval C++ loop
# (9.8 s -> 6.7 s for 3M posedges), which only brings it level with the --timing bench: Verilator's timing scheduler was never the cost.
# Conclusion: the speed is the RTL's evaluation cost per cycle (large flattened combinational cone). Getting hours-not-days needs RTL/Verilator-structure
# changes (e.g. smaller decode logic, --threads is useless on 2 cores shared with other jobs) or more cores, not a different bench.
